# Wave W17-P (Route 119): gauge pine — a rain pine in wet deep greens, tiered and drip-crowned: pale drip flecks hang under the crown’s tiers where the permanent rain runs off it, highlight lifted to the wet top, on gauge turf (ground baked in). Route 119’s own tree — split from Route 116’s dry echo pine by the drips and the deeper register: same family, opposite weather.
